{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392719-2e-scion-rp-anchors","id":1392719,"title":"[2E] Scion RP Anchors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-29T19:06:56-07:00","id":1392719,"title":"[2E] Scion RP Anchors","content":"'Anchors' are term from 2E <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> rules engine, where they mark 'basic character archetype' - things that ground the character in roleplaying way in the setting story. They are Virtue &amp; Vice, Mask &amp; Dirge, Blood &amp; Bone, etc. <b>What kind of other Anchors have characters in Scion? Are they simply their Pantheons Virtues?</b> If yes - what would be those Anchors on <b>Origin</b> tier of the game, where characters do not know their Pantheons still?<br /> <br /> In <b>CoD</b> games, I award players 0-2 Experience ( 'Beats' ) after each game session for casualy playing their Anchors. They do not need to throw themselves over the bus to get Fortitude point - only by being really persistent on issues they get. Could the similar take also work in <b>Scion</b> 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T20:04:51-07:00","id":1392733,"title":"","content":"Your character is kind of defined by their Paths. The Paths explain where you come from, who you are, what you do, they mark which skills you picked up through your life, your Paths define where you can go, who you know, their basic training, their ways of life.<br /> <br /> You gain experience from accomplishing your Deeds, so those work for defining what your character wants.<br /> <br /> If you want to play World of Darkness, you can play World of Darkness, but I don't think that it's good to port mechanics from World of Darkness into Scion. Slightly different systems, very different gamefeels, very different tones.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T04:30:40-07:00","id":1392783,"title":"","content":"While i dont think there needs a mechanical tidbit attached to it.<br /> The concept of anchors could be useful to develop your character and create people and things that matter to your scion.<br /> <br /> As Kyman point above the big element for your character are your Paths ( Origin, Role, Pantheon).<br /> <br /> What i would do is ask the player to pick an &quot;Anchor&quot;, meaning 1 important person or place or object for each of the players path.<br /> <br /> So you could have a beloved teacher for your Origin path and the Temple where you recieved your visitation for the Pantheon path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:59:38-07:00","id":1392871,"title":"","content":"Yeah like if a Path noting &quot;Kid from a single-parent household in the Bronx&quot; isn't enough of an anchor for your character, you can like... Make a note. &quot;Hates injustice&quot; or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}